{
  "id": "hicks-gallery",
  "name": "Hicks's walkway",
  "description": "The open walkway along the outside of Hicks's block on Level 2 of the Ribbon, down where the stack barely sees daylight. There's no sky: the ceiling is the rusted girders, ducts and cables of the level above, a big fan turning slowly, laundry strung under the beams. On the left, a patched steel railing over the drop to the Level 1 street, its awnings and signs glowing far below, and across the gap the next stack's wall of lit windows, with a sodium lamp hanging off a beam. On the right, the block's stained concrete wall and its row of grilled doors running away to a stair down at the far end. Hicks's door is the nearest, plain grey steel behind a grille, no number and nothing in front of it, only a camera taped above it with a red light and a caged lamp that flickers. Further down, the Zhou twins' door is covered in stickers, boots and a crate of old deck parts beside it, warm light and a screen showing through their barred window.",
